{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-118-1","title":"Psalms 118:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 An exhortation to praise God for his mercy. 5 The psalmist by his experience shews how good it is to trust in God. 19 Under the type of the psalmist the coming of Christ in his kingdom is expressed.</p>\n<p>A.M. 2962. B.C. 1042. (Title.)This Psalm was probably composed by David after Nathan's prophetic address; and sung by alternate choirs at some public festival. It largely partakes of David's spirit, and everywhere shews the hand of a master; the style is grand and sublime; the subject noble and majestic.</p>\n<p>29; 103:17; 106:1; 107:1; 136:1; 1Ch 16:8,34; Jer 33:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-2","title":"Psalms 118:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>115:9-11; 135:19,20; 145:10; 147:19,20; Ga 6:16; Heb 13:15 1Pe 2:9,10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-3","title":"Psalms 118:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>134:1-3; 1Pe 2:5; Re 1:6; 4:7-11; 5:8-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-4","title":"Psalms 118:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>22:23; Re 19:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-5","title":"Psalms 118:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>called. 18:6; 40:1-3; 77:2; 107:13,19; 116:3,4; 120:1; 130:1,2; Ge 32:7,9-11 1Sa 30:6-8; Mr 14:31-36 in distress. Heb. out of distress. 130:1 set me. 18:19; 31:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-6","title":"Psalms 118:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>The Lord. 27:1-3; 46:1,11; 56:4,9,11; 146:5; Isa 51:12; Jer 20:11; Mic 7:8-10 Ro 8:31; Heb 13:6 on my side. Heb. for me.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-7","title":"Psalms 118:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>taketh. 54:4; 55:18; 1Ch 12:18 therefore. 54:7; 59:10; 92:11; 112:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-8","title":"Psalms 118:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>40:4; 62:8,9; Jer 17:5-7; Mic 7:5-7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-9","title":"Psalms 118:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>than to put. 146:3-5; Isa 30:2,3,15-17; 31:1,8; 36:6,7; Eze 29:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-10","title":"Psalms 118:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>All nations. 2Sa 5:1-25; 8:1-18; 10:1-19; Zec 12:3; 14:1-3; Re 19:19-21; 20:8,9 destroy them. Heb. cut them off.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-11","title":"Psalms 118:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>22:12-16; 88:17; 1Sa 23:26; 1Ch 19:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-12","title":"Psalms 118:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>like bees. De 1:44 quenched. 83:14,15; Ec 7:6; Isa 27:4; Na 1:10 in the name. 8:9; 20:1,5; 1Sa 17:45; 2Sa 23:6; 1Ch 14:10,11,14-16; 2Ch 14:11,12 2Ch 16:7-9; 20:17-22; 22:7,8 destroy them. Heb. cut them down.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-13","title":"Psalms 118:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>18:17,18; 56:1-3; 1Sa 20:3; 25:29; 2Sa 17:1-3; Mic 7:8; Mt 4:1-11 Heb 2:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-14","title":"Psalms 118:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>is my strength. 18:2; Ex 15:2-6; Isa 12:2; 45:17,22-25; Mt 1:21-23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-15","title":"Psalms 118:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>voice. 30:11,12; 32:11; 33:1; 119:54,111; De 12:12; Isa 51:11; 65:13 Ac 2:46,47; 16:34; Re 18:20; 19:1-5 the right. 44:3; 45:4; 60:12; 89:13; 98:1; Isa 51:9,10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-16","title":"Psalms 118:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>right hand. Ex 15:6; Ac 2:32-36</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-17","title":"Psalms 118:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>die. 6:5; Isa 38:16-20; Hab 1:12; Joh 11:4; Ro 14:7-9 declare. 40:5,10; 71:17,18; 73:28; 107:22; 119:13; 145:4; Jer 51:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-18","title":"Psalms 118:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>chastened. 66:10-12; 94:12,13; 2Sa 12:10; 13:1-39; 16:1-23; Job 5:17,18 Job 33:16-30; Pr 3:11,12; Jon 2:6; 1Co 11:32; 2Co 1:9-11; 6:9 Heb 12:10,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-19","title":"Psalms 118:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Open. Isa 26:2; Re 22:14 I will go. 9:13,14; 66:13-15; 95:2; 100:4; 116:18,19; Isa 38:20,22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-20","title":"Psalms 118:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>This gate.Dr. Kennicott supposes that this verse was sung by the priest, the next by the king, the three next by a chorus of people, the 25th by the king, the two next by the priest, the 28th by the king, and the last the grand chorus of the whole assembly.</p>\n<p>24:3,4,7,9; Isa 26:2; 35:8-10; Re 21:24-27; 22:14,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-21","title":"Psalms 118:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>22:23,24; 69:33,34; 116:1 and art. 14; Ex 15:2; Isa 12:2; 49:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-22","title":"Psalms 118:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>The stone. Mt 21:42; Mr 12:10,11; Lu 20:17; Ac 4:11; Eph 2:20-22; 1Pe 2:4-8 the head. Zec 4:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-23","title":"Psalms 118:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>the Lord's doing. Heb. from the Lord. Ac 2:32-36; 3:14,15; 5:31,32; Eph 1:19-22 it is. Job 5:9; Ac 4:13; 13:41</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-24","title":"Psalms 118:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>the day. Zec 3:9; Mt 28:1-8; Joh 20:19,20; Ac 20:7; Re 1:10 we will. 84:10; 1Ki 8:66; 2Ch 20:26-28; Ne 8:10; Isa 58:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-25","title":"Psalms 118:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>Save. 20:9; 22:21; 69:1,13 send now. 90:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-26","title":"Psalms 118:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>Blessed. Zec 4:7; Mt 21:9; 23:39; Mr 11:9,10; Lu 19:38; Joh 12:13 we have. 134:3; Nu 6:23-26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-27","title":"Psalms 118:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>God. 1Ki 18:21,39 shewed. 18:28; 37:6; Es 8:16; Isa 9:2; 60:1; Mic 7:9; Mal 4:2; Joh 8:12 1Pe 2:9 bind. 51:18,19; 1Ki 8:63,64; 1Ch 29:21; Heb 13:15 the horns. Ex 27:2; 38:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-28","title":"Psalms 118:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>my God. 145:1; 146:2; Ex 15:2; Isa 12:2; 25:1,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-118-29","title":"Psalms 118:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":118,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":118,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>1; 103:17; Ezr 3:11; Isa 63:7</p>"}]}